## Visual concept used

A landscape **staged-commissioning run-up profile** in the locked Fit "Engineering Diagnostic Instrument" style — the chart an engineer reads when bringing a plant up to its *rated operating point* over time and holding it there rather than overclocking past nameplate. The hero is a single dominant **ratcheting sawtooth build-trace** climbing left→right across a multi-year time axis (Y1 · Y2 · Y3 · Y4–5) and **decelerating into a heavy-weighted target asymptote** (lean FFMI 28–29.5, "rated capacity" — the climb visibly flattens and stops). Each year is an on-block climb followed by a wide 3–4 month recovery **valley that banks higher than the last** (green restore lamps = muscle memory consolidating). Beneath the trace, the four 5.0 control loops run as a **maturation braid** — one strand in Y1, fanning to six in Y3 (Test → DHT-family → 19-nor, bioidentical before exotic), thinning back to two in Y4–5 — with four year-detail panels carrying the compound specifics. Two **never-off baseline rails** (blood-work cadence with tick-density tightening on-block/relaxing in valleys; the protection shield as the 5.0 veto bus stretched to 3 years) span the full width unbroken. A **ghosted grey Tetra-Force "road not taken"** diverges up through the ceiling (a choice declined, deliberately *not* red). The **single red object** is the skipped-down-period bypass wire arcing over a valley with an ✕ ("clearing ≠ restoring — the one move that breaks the arc"). Docked grace-notes: the 90% food layer band, the come-off drift tail (~75% peak held; kidney/liver asymmetry), and the "buy shield → gear → monitoring" stocking order pointing to Part 5.2.

Color discipline held to spec: monochrome slate structure/loops, authority by line-weight (the asymptote is the heaviest line), green rationed to in-band/restored states, amber for cautions (HCT ceiling, Tren-last), grey for the road-not-taken, and exactly one red.

